# output_orbit_viewer.scn — 活體牙 (phase-C of "Output camera orbit"): the Output window's 3D view can be
# ORBITED with the mouse, and Reset View puts it back. This is the end-to-end proof that a left-drag over a
# Command/Points (3D) Output view drives the session Viewer camera (output_window_orbit handleOutputOrbit →
# sw::setOutputViewCamera → the phase-B cook override → the 8 activeViewCameraForward fallback sites), so the
# rendered scene visibly rotates — through the REAL imgui draw path, not a unit test.
#
# TiXL parity: CameraSelectionHandling.AutoUseFirstCam (no Camera op selected → manipulate the
# _outputWindowViewCamera, cs:175/193) + CameraInteraction left-drag=orbit (cs:146-165) + ResetView (cs:402).
#
# Fixture: compound_smoke.swproj opens on the TERMINAL Command view (no node pinned/selected) — a particle
# ring rendered through the DEFAULT camera, exactly the fallback the Viewer override replaces. Playback is
# stopped (Pos=0), so the sim does NOT animate at rest → a frame diff after the drag is PURELY the camera.
#
# NB the capture is `full` (the Output-window preview, driven by the Viewer camera), NOT `clean` — clean.png
# is a separate raw particle target that is NOT projected through the Output Viewer camera (verified live:
# clean stayed byte-identical while the full preview visibly rotated). Only `full` sees the orbit.
#
# RED proofs:
#   - (orbit) make handleOutputOrbit's Viewer branch a no-op (drop the setOutputViewCamera push) → the drag
#     no longer moves the camera → assert_diff after the drag goes RED (preview unchanged).
#   - (reset) make resetOutputViewToDefault a no-op (drop clearOutputViewCamera) → Reset View leaves the
#     orbited preview in place → the post-reset assert_diff goes RED (frame did not change back).

open app/testdata/compound_smoke.swproj
wait 0.6

# The Reset View button exists (only drawn for a 3D Command/Points view) — proves the view-type gate picked
# the 3D branch. (RED: revert the is3DView gate so it never shows → this assert_map_has goes RED.)
assert_map_has output_reset_view_btn
echo reset-view-button-present

# Baseline: capture the Output preview of the un-orbited default-camera scene.
capture full orbit_before
echo captured-default-view

# Orbit: a big left-drag INSIDE the Output viewport (below the toolbar). Repeated so the rotation is
# unmistakable (~30° azimuth). Each drag feeds handleOutputOrbit → the session ViewCamera rotates → the
# cook fallback reads it → the ring foreshortens/rotates.
do drag 857 430 990 430
do drag 857 430 990 430
do drag 857 430 990 430
wait 0.6

# The preview MUST differ from the default view — the scene rotated (the orbit reached the render).
assert_diff orbit_before
echo orbit-rotated-the-view

# Snapshot the orbited view, then Reset View — the preview must change AGAIN (back toward the default pose:
# clearOutputViewCamera + the session camera reset). Reset View button center ≈ imgui (830, 309).
capture full orbit_after
echo captured-orbited-view
do click 830 309
wait 0.6
assert_diff orbit_after
echo reset-view-restored-default
